{
  "id": "ss.enemy.warden",
  "name": "Warden",
  "description": "A soldier bred as a door. The first cut bolted a shield onto a body and came out as three circles in a row, which is the shape half this roster already is; this one is the shield all the way back. One tapering keystone — a flat face two thirds of the canvas tall at the front, narrowing to nothing behind — so the silhouette is a cork, and nothing else in the game is a straight-edged wedge. The face is packed earth read in horizontal strata, the colour of the ground it spent its life filling, which is a problem solved with a bone rim right round it rather than avoided. Under the face is the acid vent, teal because what leaves it is `ss.enemy.shot`. In the `enraged` half that vent goes out and the face splits along its own layers: it has stopped holding the passage and started coming down it. Drawn facing +x, the game flips it. Gameplay radius 42.",
  "tags": ["ss-enemy", "boss"],
  "size": [104, 96],
  "meta": {"radius": 42},
  "parts": [
    {"id": "leg_b", "at": [-26, 26], "rot": 28, "shape": {"kind": "rect", "w": 9.4, "h": 24, "corner": 4.6}, "fill": "$carapace.dark"},
